# ADR 0003: Watch app as companion extension using HKWorkoutSession

**Date:** 2026-08-02
**Status:** Accepted

## Context
FORGE needs Apple Watch functionality for rest timer haptics, HR 
display, and set tracking during workouts. Full standalone Watch 
logging (phone-optional) is not required.

## Decision
Ship the Watch app as a companion extension. When a workout begins 
on the phone, the Watch starts its own HKWorkoutSession, which 
replaces Apple Workout for the duration of the session.

## Alternatives considered
- **Standalone Watch app:** Higher dev cost; requires WatchConnectivity 
  or CloudKit for full data model access; not needed for personal use.
- **Notifications only (no HKWorkoutSession):** Cheaper but loses 
  Activity ring integration, HR readings, and always-on display.

## Consequences
- Only one HKWorkoutSession can run at a time — FORGE replaces 
  Apple Workout during sessions. Accepted trade-off.
- Activity rings fill, HR writes to Health, workout appears in 
  Fitness app — all handled by the OS.
- Watch UI is minimal: current exercise, current set target, rest 
  timer, HR display.

